  {%- comment -%} ==================== RESULTS (3-way comparison) ====================
       Prepared image slots. Set white/rgb/lab URLs per frame in the SAMPLES array (JS below).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section id="results" class="tw:mx-auto tw:w-full tw:max-w-[1400px] tw:px-[15px] tw:py-[80px] tw:md:px-[50px] tw:md:py-[120px]">
    <div class="tw:mx-auto tw:max-w-[760px] tw:text-center">
      <p class="tw:mb-[16px] tw:text-[13px] tw:font-semibold tw:uppercase tw:tracking-[0.16em] tw:text-[#60a5fa]">The results</p>
      <h2 class="tw:text-[32px] tw:font-semibold tw:leading-[1.1] tw:tracking-[-0.02em] tw:text-white tw:md:text-[46px]">Same frame, three ways. Judge for yourself.</h2>
      <p class="tw:mx-auto tw:mt-[16px] tw:max-w-[560px] tw:text-[16px] tw:text-neutral-400">The same negative under white light, with toneLight RGB, and from a professional lab scanner. No theory — just the colour you get.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ks-compare tw:mt-[48px]">
      <div class="ks-compare__col">
        <div class="ks-compare__label">White light</div>
        <div class="ks-compare__img" data-slot="white">[ white light ]</div>
      </div>
      <div class="ks-compare__col ks-compare__col--feat">
        <div class="ks-compare__label"><span class="ks-compare__dot"></span>toneLight RGB</div>
        <div class="ks-compare__img" data-slot="rgb">[ toneLight RGB ]</div>
      </div>
