  {%- comment -%} ==================== FAQ ==================== {%- endcomment -%}
  <section id="faq" class="tw:scroll-mt-[84px] tw:border-t tw:border-white/10 tw:bg-white/[0.015]">
    <div class="tw:mx-auto tw:w-full tw:max-w-[760px] tw:px-[15px] tw:py-[80px] tw:md:px-[50px] tw:md:py-[120px]">
      <h2 class="tw:mb-[40px] tw:text-center tw:text-[32px] tw:font-semibold tw:leading-[1.1] tw:tracking-[-0.02em] tw:text-white tw:md:text-[46px]">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="tw:flex tw:flex-col tw:gap-[12px]">
        <details class="tw:group tw:rounded-[2px] tw:border tw:border-white/10 tw:bg-white/[0.02] tw:p-[20px]">
          <summary class="tw:flex tw:cursor-pointer tw:list-none tw:items-center tw:justify-between tw:text-[16px] tw:font-medium tw:text-white">Which cameras are supported?<span class="tw:ml-[16px] tw:text-neutral-500 tw:transition-transform tw:group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary>
          <p class="tw:mt-[12px] tw:text-[15px] tw:leading-[1.6] tw:text-neutral-400">Any camera with a standard remote shutter input. toneLight triggers the shutter directly and never touches your exposure settings, so metering stays in your hands. All major brands.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="tw:group tw:rounded-[2px] tw:border tw:border-white/10 tw:bg-white/[0.02] tw:p-[20px]">
          <summary class="tw:flex tw:cursor-pointer tw:list-none tw:items-center tw:justify-between tw:text-[16px] tw:font-medium tw:text-white">Does it work with 120 / medium format?<span class="tw:ml-[16px] tw:text-neutral-500 tw:transition-transform tw:group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary>
          <p class="tw:mt-[12px] tw:text-[15px] tw:leading-[1.6] tw:text-neutral-400">Yes — fully compatible with toneCarrier 120 from day one. Motorised upgrades are available for both 35 mm and 120.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="tw:group tw:rounded-[2px] tw:border tw:border-white/10 tw:bg-white/[0.02] tw:p-[20px]">
          <summary class="tw:flex tw:cursor-pointer tw:list-none tw:items-center tw:justify-between tw:text-[16px] tw:font-medium tw:text-white">How does it compare to a lab scanner?<span class="tw:ml-[16px] tw:text-neutral-500 tw:transition-transform tw:group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary>
          <p class="tw:mt-[12px] tw:text-[15px] tw:leading-[1.6] tw:text-neutral-400">For most negatives, comparable — and better in resolution and flexibility. Two honest caveats: transport is currently open-loop (a small jog every few frames), and a Bayer sensor is softer at deep red and blue than a mono camera. Both are in active development.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="tw:group tw:rounded-[2px] tw:border tw:border-white/10 tw:bg-white/[0.02] tw:p-[20px]">
          <summary class="tw:flex tw:cursor-pointer tw:list-none tw:items-center tw:justify-between tw:text-[16px] tw:font-medium tw:text-white">What about slide film / E-6?<span class="tw:ml-[16px] tw:text-neutral-500 tw:transition-transform tw:group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary>
          <p class="tw:mt-[12px] tw:text-[15px] tw:leading-[1.6] tw:text-neutral-400">toneLight has a high-CRI white mode for slides. Slides are positive, so they work like normal photos in any editor — toneScan Studio isn't required.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="tw:group tw:rounded-[2px] tw:border tw:border-white/10 tw:bg-white/[0.02] tw:p-[20px]">
          <summary class="tw:flex tw:cursor-pointer tw:list-none tw:items-center tw:justify-between tw:text-[16px] tw:font-medium tw:text-white">Do I need toneScan Studio, or can I use other software?<span class="tw:ml-[16px] tw:text-neutral-500 tw:transition-transform tw:group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary>
          <p class="tw:mt-[12px] tw:text-[15px] tw:leading-[1.6] tw:text-neutral-400">toneScan Studio is the intended workflow and what the system is built around. The three captures are standard RAW, so anyone comfortable with manual channel work can experiment elsewhere. For slides, any editor works with no extra steps.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="tw:group tw:rounded-[2px] tw:border tw:border-white/10 tw:bg-white/[0.02] tw:p-[20px]">
          <summary class="tw:flex tw:cursor-pointer tw:list-none tw:items-center tw:justify-between tw:text-[16px] tw:font-medium tw:text-white">How long does a roll take?<span class="tw:ml-[16px] tw:text-neutral-500 tw:transition-transform tw:group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary>
          <p class="tw:mt-[12px] tw:text-[15px] tw:leading-[1.6] tw:text-neutral-400">About a minute to capture in semi-auto. In hot-folder mode, toneScan Studio merges scans as they arrive, so by the time you step away from the rig the files are ready to preview.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

